      "text": "Santa Marta to Cartagena"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:fb5db666cae6efb7",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "12ab7a44f99f9f8b500b4940e611ee92f14850d850a7124de05fc38c3b2aa0ff",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261110-fu6s4admm3",
        "model": "ChatGPT"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, take a private transfer from Santa Marta to Cartagena with a Spanish-speaking driver.\n\n**Transfer time:** about 4 hours.\n\nAfter arrival and check-in at your hotel, take a private sightseeing tour of Cartagena.\n\nYou’ll see historic districts with colonial buildings and mansions on cobbled streets, the visitor district of Bocagrande with its modern hotels and restaurants, and the neighbourhoods by the city walls.\n\nContinue up La Popa Hill for a panoramic view of the city and port. The Santa Cruz convent stands at the summit.\n\nThe next stop is San Felipe de Barajas, a fortress that defended the city against pirate attacks.\n\nFor souvenirs, you can visit Las Bóvedas market in the Old Town. Its stalls and shops sell jewellery, souvenirs, hammocks and other goods.\n\nThe return route follows Avenida Santander.\n\n**Duration:** 4 hours.\n\n**Included:** admission tickets, a bilingual guide, private transport and a local medical assistance card."
    },
